      "shared_perspectives": "Across the spectrum German outlets repeatedly stress that the postponement of key energy legislation is creating investment uncertainty and slowing the expansion of renewables. At the same time there is broad agreement that rising network charges for electricity and gas will sharply increase household and industrial costs, prompting calls for cost‑containment measures. Finally, despite divergent views on the role of nuclear or gas, most commentators concur that a secure supply mix – combining renewables with reliable backup capacity – is essential to meet the 2045 climate target without endangering energy security.",
